Subject: [PATCH] feat: duct bank & structure cross-section view (click a row
 to inspect)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Third iteration of the Conduit section (claude/plan-seccion-ducteria.md) —
the dedicated design view that was gap #1 in the ductery market comparison
(claude/gaps-fibra-ducteria-networking.md), previously just a data field.

Clicking a row in either tab opens a side panel with an SVG drawn to scale
from real fields, no new schema:
- Duct Bank Runs: cross-section of the bank showing every way (`ways`
  column, already in conduit_runs) sized to `diameter_inches`. Way 1 shows
  the route's recorded fill % as an area-proportional inner fill (area
  scales with r^2, not radius, so the fill reads correctly); remaining ways
  render as open/spare capacity for a future pull.
- Structures: plan-view rectangle parsed from `size_description`'s
  "WxLxD" shorthand (the format createFiberNode already writes, e.g.
  "24x36x36"), with depth and cover rating alongside.

Known simplification carried over from the previous patch: fill % still
reflects only the first cable recorded at route creation, not a sum across
every cable sharing that duct — needs a diameter_mm column on fiber_cables
to fix properly, left as follow-up.
